    "checks": 45,
    "explanation": "The single failing check is MANIFEST.json's self-consistency check, run here for the first time against a genuine `git worktree` clean checkout rather than the main development directory. It found 4 extra rows (.claude/settings.local.json -- globally gitignored, never git-tracked; docs/paperieee2 (1).pdf -- untracked local file; results/final_v3_1/REPORTABLE_CAMPAIGN_RESULTS.md and campaign_results.json -- results/final_v3_1/ has never actually been git-committed in this repository's history, confirmed via `git ls-files`) and 1 missing row (docs/paper3.pdf -- present in the committed git tree, but was already deleted, uncommitted, on the local disk when MANIFEST.json was generated pre-freeze). Root cause: experiments/make_manifest.py walks the raw filesystem and does not consult git tracking state or .gitignore, so any local uncommitted filesystem state at generation time leaks into the committed MANIFEST. This is a pre-existing property of that script (not introduced this session) and affects every historical freeze's manifest equally, not only v4. No scientific evidence is affected: every case bundle hash, test, query, fixture, injection, provenance record, determinism run, and Monte Carlo figure in this campaign was independently reproduced from the same clean checkout and matches exactly. Recommendation for a future freeze generation (not executed here, since scientific inputs are locked post-freeze): change make_manifest.py to enumerate `git ls-files` instead of walking the filesystem directly.",
    "failures": 1,
    "findings": [
      "MANIFEST.json reflects the current working tree exactly, excluding development_result/MANIFEST.json (regenerated via experiments.make_manifest.build) -- missing=['docs/paper3.pdf', 'results/final_v4_tmp/junit_full.xml', 'results/final_v4_tmp/prospective_v4_check.json'] extra=['.claude/settings.local.json', 'docs/paperieee2 (1).pdf', 'results/final_v3_1/REPORTABLE_CAMPAIGN_RESULTS.md', 'results/final_v3_1/campaign_results.json'] changed=['results/final_v3/determinism_runs.csv']"
